<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16478" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστεμφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unmoved, unshaken,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.344
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1375
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστεμφὲς ἔχεσκε [τὸ
			σκῆπτρον</span>] he held it <i>stiff,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.219
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					812
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. οἵη νέκυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.70
				</span></i>
			. Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμεῖς ἀστεμφέως
				ἐχέμεν</span> you hold <i>fast!</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.419
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				459
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστεμφῶς τὸν βίον διενήξατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Marin.
					<u>Procl.</u>
					15
				</span></i>
			: neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστεμφές</span> as
				Adv., <i>stiffly, starkly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				4.113
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεφέλαι . . ἀ.
			μελανεῦσαι</span> dark <i>without relief,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				878
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>stiff,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιηταὶ σκληροὶ καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					579
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τελαμών</span>”
				<i>unflinching,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					13.37
				</span></i>
			; as pr. n. of a Titan, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				123
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., of a
			trap, <i>relentless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.296
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζυγός, δεσμός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.417
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.84
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.424
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Duris</span>).—Poet. word, also in
			late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				1.21
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέμβω, στέμφυλον,</span>
			Skt. <i>stabhnaā´ti</i> `supports', `holds
			fast'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
